Adaptation provenance
=====================
Upstream repository: https://github.com/linux-can/can-utils
Revision inspected: 834ceef1f1eabec67625389172eebf1050d2f42b
File: lib.c (asc2nibble, parse_canframe, snprintf_canframe and DLC mapping)
Retrieved: 2026-10-24

candump.c retains the upstream dual-license notice in full and chooses its
BSD-3-Clause option. This file must accompany binary distributions containing
this adaptation so the notice and disclaimer remain available. The portable
adaptation removes Linux socket/struct dependencies and CAN XL, uses the
application's can_frame_t, and adds bounded timestamp/channel parsing plus
strict ID, FD DLC, RTR and full-line validation. It implements a documented
candump -L subset; it does not claim general can-utils file compatibility.
